What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/<device>/pwm_period_ns
Date:		November 2026
KernelVersion:	7.4
Contact:	dri-devel@lists.freedesktop.org
Description:
		(RW) The period, in nanoseconds, of the PWM that a
		pwm-backlight device dims with. It starts as the period in
		the device tree or the platform data. Writing a period changes
		the PWM frequency and keeps the brightness, for instance to
		move the frequency out of hearing or away from a camera's
		line rate. The PWM driver may round the period; a period it
		cannot make is refused with EINVAL.

		The backlight class device links here as "device", so this is
		also /sys/class/backlight/<backlight>/device/pwm_period_ns.
